# =====================================================================
# What must never reach GitHub
# =====================================================================

# Secrets. There are none in this repo today — the publishable Supabase
# key in assets/supabase-config.js is public by design — but any .env file
# would hold the service role key, the Resend key and the Twilio token.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build output. Timestamped zips, one per build; they add megabytes and
# tell you nothing a commit does not.
dist/

# Pristine copies of images kept before compression. Useful locally,
# pointless in version control.
assets/_originals/

# Local previews with stubbed sample data. Excluded from deploys already;
# excluded here too so nobody mistakes one for a real page.
portal/_preview-*.html

# Working files that live in the project ROOT but are not the website:
# screenshots, reference images, and downloads with generated names. The
# leading slash matters — it confines these to the root and leaves
# assets/ alone, which is where the real images live.
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.png
/*.zip

node_modules/
.vercel/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Auth-free copies of portal pages, generated on the fly to test layout
# without a Supabase session. Never part of the site.
_h-*.html
_shell-harness.html
_stub-*.js
_portal-*.js
